+## WebSocket access (#144)
+
+- The WebSocket validator accepts `list_conversations` independently of configuration, strips an extra `userId`, accepts integer limits 1–200 and a complete `{updatedAt, sessionId}` cursor, and rejects invalid limits or cursors with an error naming the field ([validated by: validates history limits and complete composite cursors independently of configuration](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- With `transport.history.enabled`, a requested `conversation_list` contains only the authenticated connection owner’s four-field summaries with ISO date strings, newest first including the current session, passes `ws.userId` and `{limit, before}` unchanged to the store, pages ties without losing a row, sends no unsolicited list or `stream_end`, and lets a listed id reconnect through the existing owned-session resume and replay ([validated by: lists only the authenticated owner with wire dates, pages ties, and resumes a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L131)).
