+
+## 14. Conversation list (#144)
+
+### Client request: list_conversations
+
+| Field              | Type    | Required    | Description                                     |
+| ------------------ | ------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string  | Yes         | `"list_conversations"`                          |
+| `limit`            | integer | No          | 1–200; store default when absent                |
+| `before`           | object  | No          | Composite cursor from the last summary received |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string  | With cursor | ISO timestamp accepted by `Date.parse`          |
+| `before.sessionId` | string  | With cursor | Session id breaking ties on activity            |
+
+The validator accepts the request independently of the history flag and rejects malformed limits or incomplete cursors with a field-specific error ([validated by: validates history limits and complete composite cursors independently of configuration](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+
+### Server response: conversation_list
+
+| Field                        | Type   | Description                                           |
+| ---------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                       | string | `"conversation_list"`                                 |
+| `conversations`              | array  | Summaries in descending activity and session-id order |
+| `conversations[].sessionId`  | string | Id to reconnect with through `?sessionId=<id>`        |
+| `conversations[].createdAt`  | string | ISO creation time                                     |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt`  | string | ISO last-activity time                                |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | number | Entry count, with no entry content                    |
+
+**GDPR:** a list discloses one authenticated user's own conversation metadata and no conversation content or credentials; identity comes from the connection, never the frame, and `transport.history` is the deployer's explicit decision to make this data reachable from the client ([validated by: lists only the authenticated owner with wire dates, pages ties, and resumes a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L131)).
+
+One list is sent only when requested, with no `stream_end`, and its paging cursor retains the session-id tie-break; selecting a listed id uses existing ownership-checked resume and replay ([validated by: lists only the authenticated owner with wire dates, pages ties, and resumes a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L131)).
+
+History defaults off independently of resume, and disabled or unavailable listing returns `UNSUPPORTED` instead of an empty history ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED for disabled history and stores or collections unable to list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L174)).
+
+Store failures return a safe `SERVER_ERROR` and are logged with session context without content, leaving the socket open ([validated by: contains a real store rejection in one safe SERVER_ERROR and logs its session without user content](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L207)).
+
+History requests bypass the turn lock and are answered before an unfinished turn ends ([validated by: answers history while the same session has an unfinished turn holding its lock](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L231)).
